f48069227c7a08ae5a04508e0596586358243eecb2a97","event_uuid":"0e57f19a-8ad5-41c9-996a-179baf2a20ac","position":{"commit_sha":"96ef17edd2f3abecfbede25236dc3bcefa52422f","position":"1788921589420718001-0e57f19a-8ad5-41c9-996a-179baf2a20ac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-authorized AC remediation for Phase 2 closeout: AC9 depended on the review bot performing its first post-window write, an external event an executing agent cannot trigger. The original problem remains addressed by the reclaim/epoch-guard/off-repo-backup scope; AC9 is restated as an operator follow-up evidence item rather than an in-session close blocker.","timestamp":1788874884825014001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 closeout: all direct children are now closed. calm-dutybound-drongo was dispositioned no-code/obsolete after existing production suppression evidence; unappeased-inaccurate-narwhal was closed obsolete because the A6-1 reclaim execution already consumed the ref-hygiene/off-repo-bundle protocol. Marking epic ACs complete to reflect landed child evidence plus operator-authorized remediation of external post-window checks.","timestamp":1788886026104931001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 closeout attempted after all children closed and plan review certified. Normal close is blocked by the known task/epic close-gate reference scan: it reports no commit referencing the epic or descendants even though the epic is an aggregate over already-closed child work and this closeout made no code change. Per instruction, I am not forcing this; leaving for the close-gate follow-up.","timestamp":1788887145596353001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close precheck after the reference-scan fix surfaced one real file-impact drift item: descendant implementation commit f83fe247 also added scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py for the GET rotation sidecar cutover proof. Added that path to the epic file_impact; this is material, so I am refreshing plan review before retrying close.","timestamp":1788920940737049001}],"created_at":1788158688930308001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[],"description":"Reduce rebar tickets-store growth and reclaim the ~1 GiB already spent, by making the\nreconciler's committed `.bridge_state` cache cheap instead of re-homing it.\n\nMeasured facts, full research trail and the three corrected false premises: session_log\n**1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (dinky-frowsy-woodborer). Supersedes the tabled plan in\n**bronze-used-foxhound** (e594-e1d0). Umbrella: **1270-b740**.\n\n## Context\n\nThe `tickets` branch is **1.04 GiB**; **92%** is the reconciler's `.bridge_state` cache, not\nticket data (events are 55 MB). Diffing consecutive committed revisions of `bindings.json`\n(1509 bindings) shows the growth is bookkeeping nothing reads:\n\n| field | entries changed per pass |\n|---|---|\n| `baseline` (the value) | **0** |\n| `baseline_advanced_at` (written at `binding_store.py:375`, read nowhere in `src/`) | **1144** |\n| `last_get_pass` (rotation bookkeeping) | **20** |\n\nA scattered edit across a sort-ordered 18 MB file defeats git delta compression. Measured on 40\nconsecutive real revisions rebuilt in a clean repo and repacked `--window=250 --depth=50`, true\nmarginal cost per version is **12.79 KB** today, **1.74 KB** after deleting the timestamp (7.4x),\nand the version count halves once rotation bookkeeping moves out (12.8x total).\n\n## Approach and why this one\n\nKeep the cache committed and make it cheap. `.bridge_state` must stay on-branch because the\nreconciler runs on **ephemeral** GitHub-hosted runners, so durable state has to live in git — an\nearlier design wrote prev to the main-branch worktree, so prev was always `{}` and the differ\nre-derived 2050+ inbound creates every pass (`reconcile.py:258-259`). Epic `6c9c` evaluated and\ndropped re-homing it off-branch (WS-1) because the convergence loop already self-heals binding\ndrift. So the levers are content and churn, not location.\n\nThe one-time reclaim of existing history is included (child A6) under an operator-approved\nquiescence protocol. Its mechanics are **proven, not theoretical**: `git fast-export --no-data |\nfilter | git fast-import` on the real branch produced 1,172,586,762 -> 98,803,422 bytes (8.4%)\nwith all 49,888 commits and 2,661 merges preserved and the HEAD tree byte-identical except the\nintended paths. Stock git plumbing only — `git-filter-repo` is deliberately **not** used: it is an\nunwanted core dependency and it prunes empty commits, which would reshape the DAG that\nancestry-based authorship verification walks.\n\n## Scope (children, in dependency order)\n\n1. **A1** delete `baseline_advanced_at` + write-when-changed guard in `set_baseline`\n2. **A2-1** move `last_get_pass` to `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json`; read `max(new, legacy)`\n3. **A3** text-normalize baseline description/status/priority (exclude `assignee`)\n4. **A2-2** delete the legacy in-line `last_get_pass` field (gated on writer rollout)\n5. **A4-1/2/3** `bridge_fsck` fence, then `prev_snapshot` -> key-set, then branch-3 empty-payload skip\n6. **A5** ADR covering all three committed-format changes\n7. **A6** one-time reclaim under the quiescence protocol (LAST; requires A1-A5 and Epic B's B6)\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nThree committed-format changes to a shared store file, each with a stated boundary. A2-1 is\nreversible (it never stops writing the legacy field). A3 is reversible because the read path\ncanonicalizes both shapes idempotently. A2-2 and A4-2 are the irreversible steps: A2-2 is gated on\nobserved writer rollout; reverting A4-2 requires the reverse-direction corpus diff recorded first.\nA6 is gated on an off-repo backup bundle plus a fail-closed epoch guard, and its resumability is\nexplicitly **none** — mitigated by running every correctness assertion on a scratch clone before\nanything is published.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Marginal packed cost per changed `bindings.json` version is **<=25% of the pre-change\n      baseline measured by the same method** (rebuild N>=40 consecutive revisions in a clean repo,\n      repack `--window=250 --depth=50`, compute `(pack_N - pack_1)/(N-1)`). Baseline today 12.79 KB.\n      Verify: the measurement script recorded in the child ticket.\n- [x] Two consecutive reconciler passes over unchanged Jira state produce a **byte-identical**\n      `bindings.json` and create **no commit**. Tier: integration against a stateful fake asserting\n      file bytes and commit count, not call counts.\n- [x] `baseline_advanced_at` is absent from every entry written by `set_baseline`, and no `src/`\n      reference to it remains. Verify: `grep -r baseline_advanced_at src/` returns nothing.\n- [x] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves the worktree byte-identical\n      (`git status --porcelain` empty) — the read-only path must not persist a migration.\n- [x] A **dict-shaped** baseline fed through the live `compute_update_fields` path yields the same\n      verdict as its normalized-string equivalent. This test does not exist today; the existing\n      cells use flat strings only, so a no-op-on-strings normalizer would pass while proving\n      nothing. Tier: integration through the real production comparison path.\n- [x] Corpus mutation-diff (full prev vs key-set prev) over >=4 real snapshot pairs shows zero\n      difference in any mutation reaching Jira with a non-empty effect, **and** the reverse-direction\n      diff is recorded as the A4-2 rollback artifact.\n- [x] `outbound_differ.py` is **<=800 LOC** after the rotation extraction (it is at exactly 800\n      today; the locked module-size gate fails the build on 801).\n- [x] A fresh **unfiltered** clone of `tickets` is **<=150 MB**, `HEAD^{tree}` equals the recorded\n      pre-rewrite tip tree, and commit and merge-commit counts are unchanged (measured at window\n      time, not hardcoded).\n- [x] The reclaim window records the post-window non-resurrection check as an operator follow-up:\n      after the first review-bot write that actually occurs, `git merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip>\n      origin/tickets` is false and `size-pack` growth is <1 MB. This is not an in-session close\n      blocker because the triggering write is an external operational event; the closeable scope is\n      the guarded reclaim, backup, and stale-epoch prevention that make resurrection detectable and\n      preventable.\n- [x] A clone on a stale epoch attempting to push **aborts and performs no merge** at **both**\n      guarded sites (`sync._union_merge` and `push.py`'s non-FF retry). Tier: integration in two\n      real temporary clones with divergent epochs.\n- [x] An ADR exists enumerating all three committed-format changes, the mixed-version protocol, the\n      A2-2 gate, and each rollback boundary.\n- [x] The off-repo backup bundle exists and `git bundle verify` passes. **[operator-attested]**\n- [x] Operator has confirmed zero active sessions and all `rebar-mcp` servers stopped before the\n      reclaim window. **[operator-attested]**","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"baseline guard + rotation extraction + normalization"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"_advance_baselines caller; prev persist"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py","reason":"branch-3 empty-payload skip"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/sync.py","reason":"epoch guard at _union_merge"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"epoch guard before its own merges"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"epoch field + remote-side reader"},{"path":"scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py","reason":"GET rotation sidecar cutover measurement script changed by descendant implementation commit f83fe247."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5fec159a-72d9-46f3-a64f-0cfba647edeb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Bound tickets-store growth: make the committed .bridge_state cache cheap + one-time reclaim of the spent ~1 GiB","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4432e8a5-5f01-479e-afc4-61e7b4ee5d9c","61a2ef38-9188-4017-b070-375a63f4584b","17d24929-3333-4a7e-9043-dbf9255657bc","5fec159a-72d9-46f3-a64f-0cfba647edeb","f251856d-9eae-46fc-ad07-22a50ed967b7","62b62023-f2a2-4216-ad64-5361715887ae","876b74c0-ce5c-4f8c-85ba-1d0ec004874f","d0224be0-7aba-4a41-946f-fa519da2744d","9d6ecb49-341e-4e25-927f-22d8b9d3042d","be065dd4-ed6f-4d9f-a128-c6b2d407d3d7","76e5a324-1839-4abc-9108-dd677536610a","0e57f19a-8ad5-41c9-996a-179baf2a20ac"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788921589420718002,"uuid":"cecfe399-45fd-4f3e-a78e-ee0766eec3c8"}